course: dictionary
lesson: 3279
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You can work out which meaning is right by reading the words around it. Eruption is a good example: it can be about a volcano, a burst of laughter, or spots on the skin.
explain: «A volcano is an opening in the crust where melted rock, gas and ash escape from inside the Earth.» The clues are volcano, rock and ash, so eruption here means a volcano suddenly throwing out lava, ash and gas.
explain: «The room went quiet, then came an eruption of laughter.» There is no volcano here, and laughter is not a rock. The clue is laughter, so eruption means a sudden burst of something. Always test your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: An eruption is a sudden burst. A volcano erupts when it suddenly throws out lava, ash, rocks and gas.
fact: «Eruption» can also mean a sudden burst of noise, laughter, anger or fighting.
fact: On the skin, an eruption is a sudden rash or spots.
fact: «Krakatoa's eruption in 1883 was heard nearly 5,000 km away.»
fact: Igneous rocks form when molten rock cools and hardens, either deep underground or on the surface after an eruption.
exercise: «The 2010 eruption of Eyjafjallajökull in Iceland grounded most flights across Europe.» What is the eruption here? | *A volcano suddenly throwing out ash | A sudden burst of laughter | A loud noise from a football crowd | A rash on the skin
exercise: «The room went quiet, then came an eruption of laughter.» What does eruption mean here? | A volcano throwing out lava | A slow, gentle breeze | *A sudden burst of laughter | A sore red rash
exercise: Mum says the doctor found an eruption on Sam's arm. What does eruption mean? | A sunny morning walk | A river of melted rock | A deep, cold lake | *A sudden rash or spots
test: What is a volcanic eruption? | *A volcano suddenly throwing out lava, ash, rocks and gas | A sudden fall of snow down a mountain | A river running into the sea | A tall tree in a forest
test: Which meaning of eruption fits «Krakatoa's eruption in 1883 was heard nearly 5,000 km away»? | A kind of soft rock | *A volcano suddenly throwing out lava, ash and gas | A sudden burst of laughter | A rash on the skin
exam: Sam says eruption always means a volcano. Is Sam right? | *No, it can also mean a sudden burst of laughter, anger or noise | Yes, but only in science lessons | Yes, it only ever means a volcano | No, it only means a rash on the skin
